Z||000000||ChadMan||07-17-2001||10:46 AM||||This is kind of a shot in the dark.  I have a 1982 Yamaha Maxim XJ750 - looks great, runs great, low miles.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/lwf2.jpg"> <P>However, the instruments are all screwed up.  The speedo reads 15-20 mph low, the tach is "lazy" (never goes above 4K, even when I wind the bike out) and the fuel gage gives me a false empty most of the time.<P>I am lousy with electrical systems, so I have no idea where to begin.  Any ideas?||||reg||5
Z||000001||Ken Wittlief||07-17-2001||10:53 AM||||Electronic that fail after a long peroid are due to poor connections 95% of the time.<P>  since you have several gauges that are 'screwed up' I would start looking for a common connector they all share - pull the connectors apart and clean the contacts if they are corroded.<P>  could also be a bad ground wire connection - maybe all the instruments share a single ground wire to the frame - and its broken or rusty.<P>  -Ken BSEE (normal consulting fee is $100/hr - this ones on the house :c)||||reg||1
Z||000002||84Bill||07-17-2001||11:07 AM||||yup, sounds like a bad ground||||reg||1
Z||000003||Cliff Pennock||07-17-2001||04:14 PM||||Bad ground was my first guess also.||||reg||1
Z||000004||isthiswhereiputausername?||07-17-2001||04:57 PM||||Dont they have the cable speedo?<P>cable could be slipping..   try to check to see if its tight..<P>other things?<P>bad ground is my guess too||||reg||1
Z||000005||Monkeyman||07-17-2001||09:55 PM||||Chad--I have an '86 Suzuki Intruder.  Once I get my own electrical problem figured out (I think it's the rectifier--headlight and speedo go dim/bright/dim/bright, but rpms don't seem to affect it) we'll have to meet in the middle and go riding.<P>Once I wipe the sawdust off of it, I'll snap a pic and post it.  Nice bike.  Drag bars, forward controls, side mounted plate holder/tail light, etc.  I'll lower the rear and recover the seats this winter.<P>------------------<BR>'Consciousness:  That annoying time between naps.'<P>MM||||reg||1
Z||000006||ChadMan||07-18-2001||09:18 AM||||Bad ground?  Gee, that sounds like work.  Maybe I should just trade the bike to BOILERMAKER...   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Monkeyman, that sounds like fun.  All my riding buddies "grew up" and sold their bikes.  Intruder...is that an 800cc twin?<P>My Maxim is heavy and not the best handling bike, but man, does it eat up highway miles.  It is the most comfortable cruising bike I've ever ridden (though I've never ridden a Gold Wing).||||reg||1
